  "composer": {
    "rawText": "[Song Title: Offset That Wouldn’t Clear]\r\n[Style: math rock, electronic hybrid, glitch-forward, clean studio recording, interlocking clean guitars, odd-meter live drums, tight bass, modular synth glitches, bitcrush artifacts, sparse expressive male vocal, intentional errors, misfires, dropouts]\r\n[Caption: The mistake repeats until it becomes the rule.]\r\n[Image: A waveform with one recurring spike slightly out of place.]\r\n[Refresh Title: Random 5]\r\n[Theme: Random]\r\n[Gradients: 5]\r\n[Rank: 22]\r\n[Title Rarity: 1.12]\r\n[Seeds: intentionally unstable]\r\n[Perspective: system_voice]\r\n[Concept: A process encounters an error it cannot fully resolve—and keeps going anyway.]\r\n[Topic: System & Process → error_persistence]\r\n[Genre Bias: math_rock → electro_modern]\r\n[Style Change: none]\r\n[Modulation: none]\r\n[Hook Prominence: low]\r\n[Deviation: error-driven composition]\r\n[Composer Version: v2.3]\r\n\r\n[Intro]\r\n[Guitars enter clean in 4, drums enter late in 7.]\r\n[A synth click fires one beat early—this is unintentional, but repeats.]\r\n[NOTE (unsung clue): the system logs the error but does not halt.]\r\n\r\n[Section A]\r\n[Drums lock into 13/8; guitars phrase confidently in 12.]\r\n[Bass follows the drums, not the guitars.]\r\n[A short digital glitch appears at the end of every second bar.]\r\nI lined it up, I checked it twice  \r\nStill something slipped between  \r\nThe numbers said it should be fine  \r\nBut that’s not what I’m seeing\r\n\r\n[Section A’]\r\n[Same as Section A, but the glitch occurs every bar now.]\r\n[Guitars drop one note consistently in the same place.]\r\n[Synth briefly mutes for exactly one beat, every loop.]\r\nIt wasn’t wrong enough to fail  \r\nIt wasn’t right enough to pass  \r\nSo it stayed inside the system  \r\nLike a question I can’t ask\r\n\r\n[Section B]\r\n[Sudden shift to 9/8 without transition.]\r\n[Drums and bass align; guitars lag by half a beat.]\r\n[A buffer crackle appears whenever vocals stop.]\r\nI tried to roll it back again  \r\nBut every copy kept the scar  \r\nThe fix just taught the fault  \r\nExactly where the limits are\r\n\r\n[Interference]\r\n[All instruments drop except a looping glitch fragment.]\r\n[The fragment is five beats long against implied four.]\r\n[NOTE (unsung clue): this fragment is the original error, isolated.]\r\n\r\n[Section C]\r\n[Full band returns, but everything feels slightly misaligned.]\r\n[Drums accent the wrong beat on purpose.]\r\n[Guitars mirror the error fragment as a motif.]\r\nIt doesn’t crash, it doesn’t end  \r\nIt just repeats another way  \r\nLike something learned the wrong lesson  \r\nAnd refuses to unlearn the day\r\n\r\n[Break]\r\n[Hard cut—silence for less than a full bar.]\r\n[Restart is one tick late.]\r\n[NOTE (unsung clue): timing reference has drifted.]\r\n\r\n[Final Section]\r\n[All parts layer densely; glitches now feel intentional.]\r\n[The original error becomes the rhythmic anchor.]\r\n[Nothing resolves, but everything stabilizes.]\r\nI stopped trying to correct it  \r\nLet the fault define the frame  \r\nIf it runs, it runs imperfect  \r\nBut it runs the same\r\n\r\n[Ending]\r\n[Instruments drop out randomly, not by section order.]\r\n[Final sound is the glitch fragment, clean and centered.]\r\n[NOTE (unsung clue): the bug has been promoted to feature.]\r\n",
